<div class="rich-text w-full"><p>About 80% of Indian warehouses lack automation, which leads to inventory losses and reduced throughput. Our vision for smart warehouse automation goes far beyond traditional inventory management.</p></div>
<div class="rich-text w-full"><p>We are building intelligent, IoT-enabled systems that optimize every step of warehouse operations, from goods receipt to order fulfillment, using real-time data, robotics, and artificial intelligence.</p></div>
<div class="rich-text w-full"><h2>What we are building</h2></div>
<div class="rich-text w-full"><ul><li><strong>Automated goods receiving and put-away</strong>, so stock is checked in and stored without manual bottlenecks.</li><li><strong>Robotic goods movement</strong> with automated guided vehicles (AGVs) and autonomous mobile robots (AMRs).</li><li><strong>Voice-guided and AR-assisted picking</strong> to help warehouse staff work faster and with fewer mistakes.</li><li><strong>AI-based inventory management</strong> that predicts stock needs with demand forecasting algorithms.</li></ul></div>
<div class="rich-text w-full"><h2>The impact</h2></div>
<div class="rich-text w-full"><p>IoT and robotics can improve order fulfillment by 40% and reduce errors by 25%. Combined with barcode and RFID tracking, dock and dispatch scheduling, and warehouse-to-vehicle coordination in Next Fleet, the warehouse becomes a fully connected part of the supply chain.</p></div>
